vity of Divisibility"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e1582c6-f975-57a2-bb84-29de70274193" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420196} {:answer/id #uuid "5d34d488-7731-54e1-adee-10ba7466acca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420208} {:answer/id #uuid "6b4b7a2b-3e52-5afd-8b75-c581575d9429" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420213} {:answer/id #uuid "86a84e34-cc31-5936-aa5b-9bcfb65473f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420218} {:answer/id #uuid "a39f6118-e6af-5c4f-b439-8c10db5598d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420222}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b4b7a2b-3e52-5afd-8b75-c581575d9429" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420213} :answer-field/id #uuid "185758a4-16ad-57b8-bf67-872651eda925" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420244}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "73c135de-ad71-58aa-a780-c01d04341240" :question/math-academy-id "q-221379" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If $12∣h$ then $4∣h$\n- If $4∣h$ then $2∣h$\n- If $3∣h$ then $12∣h$" :question/worked-solution "For any integers $a,$ $b,$ and $c,$ we have transitivity of divisibility:\n\n$a∣b\\,$ and $\\,b∣c$ $\\,⟹\\,$ $a∣c$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. First, note that $4∣12.$ Therefore, we have\n$4∣12$ and $12∣h,$ which implies that $4∣h.$\n\n- Statement II is true. First, note that $2∣4.$ Therefore, we have\n$2∣4$ and $4∣h,$ which implies that $2∣h.$\n\n- Statement III is false. As a counterexample, let $h=3.$ Then, $3∣3$ but $12∤3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420258 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198309 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7eb430d5-5241-56a2-96be-73f44b0f2114" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Transitivity of Divisibility"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37d1ed1f-2a27-5962-9f76-7e68504f6b25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420198} {:answer/id #uuid "92f86242-b5e9-5e13-99b0-1f387aeb933c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420220} {:answer/id #uuid "a873a377-31d6-5d14-bc3d-af2b01b12bb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420223} {:answer/id #uuid "d6e70fa3-3d87-548c-a566-669bf0527f26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420232} {:answer/id #uuid "f5c3abe4-7795-5469-8fa0-9b120fc335e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420242}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37d1ed1f-2a27-5962-9f76-7e68504f6b25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420198} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4feefa3-f467-563c-b592-67d4467afe30" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420251}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "24815c66-50ab-5aab-ac7b-25ddc673e132" :question/math-academy-id "q-221381" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If $11∣k$ then $33∣k$\n- If $33∣k$ then $11∣k$\n- If $33∣k$ then $3∣k$" :question/worked-solution "For any integers $a,$ $b,$ and $c,$ we have transitivity of divisibility:\n\n$a∣b\\,$ and $\\,b∣c$ $\\,⟹\\,$ $a∣c$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. As a counterexample, let $k=11.$ Then, $11∣11$ but $33∤11.$\n\n- Statement II is true. First, note that $11∣33.$ Therefore, we have\n$11∣33$ and $33∣k,$ which implies that $11∣k.$\n\n- Statement III is true. First, note that $3∣33.$ Therefore, we have\n$3∣33$ and $33∣k,$ which implies that $3∣k.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186420259 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198310 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6b3101aa-ee9e-5940-b170-2f4e78802150" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Divisibility of a Product"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d09c58ba-862c-5f52-9a82-407eb4fee047" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z∣y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420231} {:answer/id #uuid "ddc98e66-62d2-5aa0-9475-2f7fbae5b455" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x∣y" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420237} {:answer/id #uuid "ee650b6b-e854-5b04-a1a9-30be4e65f6a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y∣x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186420241} {:answer/id #uuid "f856dcae-92c9-5858-9779-1ac42a6dac11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y∣z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186